Subject: [PATCH] avformat/tcp: keep an IPv4 literal beside its NAT64 synthesis

tcp_open() resolves with AF_UNSPEC and zero ai_flags. Apple's
getaddrinfo() replaces zero flags with AI_DEFAULT (AI_V4MAPPED_CFG |
AI_ADDRCONFIG), and on a NAT64 network it answers an IPv4 literal with
addresses synthesized under the network's prefix (64:ff9b::/96). It adds
the literal itself to that answer only when AI_ADDRCONFIG is clear
(Libinfo _gai_nat64_synthesis()), so ffmpeg gets the synthesized
addresses alone.

That is wrong whenever the IPv4 address is reachable without the
carrier's NAT64 gateway -- above all through a VPN that routes it, like
Tailscale's 100.64.0.0/10. The synthesized destination leaves over
cellular, never reaches the tunnel, and the connect hangs until the open
timeout. Plezy hits this on iPhones on IPv6-only carriers with a
Jellyfin server added by its Tailscale IP (edde746/plezy#2460): the
app's own requests connect to the literal directly and work, while every
mpv open times out before the first byte.

Pass AI_NUMERICSERV, which the always-numeric portstr satisfies anyway.
Nonzero flags keep AI_DEFAULT out, so the literal joins the synthesized
addresses in the answer and ff_connect_parallel() races both families,
starting the next attempt within 200 ms. Networks without a NAT64
prefix still get the literal alone, and a public IPv4 literal on an
IPv6-only network still reaches its synthesized address.

Verified on n8.0.1 with a host ffprobe on macOS and Libinfo's NAT64 hook
emulating a 64:ff9b::/96 network: an IPv4 literal served on the LAN
resolved to 64:ff9b::c0a8:107 alone and failed without the patch, and
resolved to both and connected over IPv4 with it; a literal reachable
only through the emulated NAT64 path still connected through it. Apple
only, since other resolvers do not rewrite zero flags. Not upstream
yet.

diff --git a/libavformat/tcp.c b/libavformat/tcp.c
--- a/libavformat/tcp.c
+++ b/libavformat/tcp.c
@@ -195,6 +195,15 @@ static int tcp_open(URLContext *h, const char *uri, int flags)
     hints.ai_family = AF_UNSPEC;
     hints.ai_socktype = SOCK_STREAM;
     snprintf(portstr, sizeof(portstr), "%d", port);
+    /* portstr is always numeric. Saying so also keeps the flags nonzero:
+     * Apple's getaddrinfo() replaces zero flags with AI_DEFAULT, whose
+     * AI_ADDRCONFIG makes an IPv4 literal on a NAT64 network resolve to the
+     * synthesized 64:ff9b::/96 addresses alone. Those leave through the
+     * NAT64 gateway, never through a VPN that routes the IPv4 address itself
+     * (Tailscale's 100.64.0.0/10), and that connection hangs. Without
+     * AI_ADDRCONFIG the IPv4 address joins them in the list and
+     * ff_connect_parallel() races it against them. */
+    hints.ai_flags = AI_NUMERICSERV;
     if (s->listen)
         hints.ai_flags |= AI_PASSIVE;
     if (!hostname[0])
